  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive). No pair verb. Pattern: X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{歌|うた}う (sing X).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates ongoing action. {歌|うた}っている = 'is singing.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{歌|うた}→歌：02179_uta⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{歌|うた}う (sing a song)\n- ⟦カラオケ→カラオケ：05080_karaoke⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{歌|うた}う (sing at karaoke)\n- ⟦{上手|じょうず}→上手：00707_jouzu⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{歌|うた}う (sing well)\n- {歌|うた}い⟦{方|かた}→方：10665_kata⟧ (way of singing)\n\nCOGNATE OBJECT: ⟦{歌|うた}→歌：02179_uta⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{歌|うた}う repeats the same kanji and sounds redundant in English, but it is the normal Japanese phrasing whenever the song is not otherwise specified. With a named song the object simply replaces it.\n\nIn Japan, ⟦カラオケ→カラオケ：05080_karaoke⟧ is a popular pastime, so this verb is commonly used. A person who sings professionally is a ⟦{歌手|かしゅ}→歌手：00197_kashu⟧.",
